From 0bc8917e0b6a99885fdfcbf0e4984fa17463c03c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rolotrealanis98 <122947376+rolotrealanis98@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:27:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] kboot: n1: fill the T6050 N1 hand-off in the DT

The protocol-27 centauri driver and pcie-apple's T6050 adoption need from
the boot loader what only the ADT knows. For the apple,t6050-pcie host:

- the N1 control function (pci106b,1900) gets firmware-name
  "apple/centauri/<target-type>-ftab.bin", apple,centauri-platform-id
  (board-id << 16 | chip-id) and apple,centauri-protocol 27 if unset;
- each apple,link-trained-by-bootloader root port gets the ADT
  pci-bridge<n> config, rc and gen3/4/5 shadow tunables as
  (offset, 4, mask, value) groups, which Linux replays in the root-port
  reset of the N1's post-ROM port cycle;
- each such root port and the DART its endpoint maps to are enabled only
  if the link is up as the adoption requires (root complex running, port
  ready, link up and not retraining, LTSSM on), numbering the root
  port's buses if they are 0; otherwise both stay disabled, since the DART
  of a port that is not up takes an SError when Linux probes it.

The MAC addresses already travel through the wifi0/bluetooth0 aliases.
Nothing here trains a link.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
